Test coverage for what changed: both new modules carry their own unit tests.
The test scaffolding that builds a picture out of rows of characters is not
tested in its own right; it is exercised by every raster test that uses it,
and a fault in it would fail those rather than hide behind them.

Visual verification: the transforms were rendered inside the real runtime on
the real sample character and the sheet was looked at. That is what found the
defect corrected in this commit - a lean that silently dropped the rows that
travelled furthest. The unit tests could not have found it, because a picture
three characters wide never runs out of room.

After the correction the sheet shows all four panels whole: the original, the
mirror, the translation clipped at its frame as designed, and the lean carrying
the whole figure with nothing lost. Every colour in every panel comes from the
sample's own palette, which the tests also enforce as a rule rather than an
observation.
